      "content": "For the cooling stage, cooked chicken should be reduced in temperature from 60°C to 21°C (140°F to 70°F) within two hours. After reducing to 21°C, it should be cooled further to 4°C (39°F) or lower within an additional four hours, totaling six hours. This rapid cooling process helps prevent the growth of Clostridium perfringens and ensures food safety. Implementing these temperature and time controls in your HACCP plan is crucial.",
